Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
6planes.nb : the second-quantized Pin(4,4) spinor field dirac16complex, its \
6-planes, gravity, Kohn-Sham pair creation and Einstein-Rosen bridges\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"1a13f3cd-cf5e-499e-b248-b19f6246316f"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook is built on Patrick L. Nash's notebook Pre-gravity6plane.nb \
((C) 2022, GNU General Public License) and mirrors its calculations for a NEW \
field, dirac16complex: a 16-component Pin(4,4) spinor field whose 16 complex \
components are anticommuting Grassmann variables (a second-quantized fermion \
field). Every matrix used below is defined exactly as in Pre-gravity6plane.nb \
and is checked entry-by-entry against that notebook's stored outputs (see the \
companion verification scripts in the repository).
The notebook is self-contained: evaluate it from top to bottom (Evaluation > \
Evaluate Notebook). All code is plain Wolfram Language; no external packages \
are loaded.
Reading guide for a beginning student: Part 1 builds the eight real 16x16 \
Dirac matrices (T16^A)[0..7]; Part 2 builds a tiny Grassmann-algebra engine; \
Part 3 defines dirac16complex and its Lagrangian; Part 4 mirrors the old \
notebook (field equations, couplings, exact solutions, light-like quanta, \
7-planes and 6-planes); Parts 5-8 are the appended gravitational, Kohn-Sham \
(DFT) and Einstein-Rosen calculations.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8af06b82-060d-450a-8f3a-69d51d7eabbb"],

Cell["Part 0. Coordinates and conventions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"461bcc1f-974d-4d1c-b141-054ee079d8da"],

Cell["\<\
The Cartesian coordinates of the project are X = {x0, x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6, \
x7}: x0 = hidden space, x1..x3 = 3-space, x4 = time, x5..x7 = superluminal \
(\"deflating\") time. The flat metric is eta4488 = \
diag(+1,+1,+1,+1,-1,-1,-1,-1), exactly as in Pre-gravity6plane.nb.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e0f35352-135b-479b-8e4e-919b7d0973a4"],

Cell["\<\
ClearAll[\"Global`*\"];
X = {x0, x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6, x7};
eta4488 = ArrayFlatten[{{IdentityMatrix[4], 0}, {0, -IdentityMatrix[4]}}];
ID4 = IdentityMatrix[4]; ID8 = IdentityMatrix[8]; ID16 = IdentityMatrix[16];
Diagonal[eta4488]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ff12f780-95de-49b5-87cc-2fcdc948ac9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "1", ",", "1", ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[1]=",ExpressionUUID->"996190bd-54bd-4df3-964f-fe85715133cf"],

Cell["Part 1. The eight real 16x16 Dirac matrices (T16^A)[0..7]", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"91c1a5c7-98a8-45ce-aa6e-3e880d3f9225"],

Cell["1.1 Exact construction (identical to Pre-gravity6plane.nb)", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f6948785-7f9a-453d-a140-075f5218cc4b"],

Cell["\<\
Spinor metric sigma (8x8), self-dual (s4by4) and anti-self-dual (t4by4) 4x4 \
matrices, the six antisymmetric 8x8 matrices, tau[A], taubar[A] = \
sigma.Transpose[sigma.tau[A]], and finally (T16^A)[A] = [[0, taubar[A]], \
[tau[A], 0]]. In this notebook the symbol T16A[A] stands for (T16^A)[A] of \
Pre-gravity6plane.nb (the old notebook used the Notation package to make \
T16^A a symbol; here we use the plain name T16A to keep the notebook \
package-free).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"403d5953-7c64-43c5-8a79-7a2b09d75f6b"],

Cell["\<\
sigma = ArrayFlatten[{{ConstantArray[0, {4, 4}], ID4}, {ID4, ConstantArray[0, \
{4, 4}]}}];
Qa[h_, p_, q_] := Signature[{h, p, q, 4}];
Qb[h_, p_, q_] := ID4[[p, 4]]*ID4[[q, h]] - ID4[[p, h]]*ID4[[q, 4]];
s4by4[h_] := Table[Qa[h, p, q] - Qb[h, p, q], {p, 4}, {q, 4}];   (* self-dual \
antisymmetric *)
t4by4[h_] := Table[Qa[h, p, q] + Qb[h, p, q], {p, 4}, {q, 4}];   (* \
anti-self-dual antisymmetric *)
sixAntiSymmetric8by8 = Flatten[{Table[ArrayFlatten[{{0, s4by4[h]}, {s4by4[h], \
0}}], {h, 1, 3}],
    Table[ArrayFlatten[{{0, t4by4[h]}, {-t4by4[h], 0}}], {h, 3, 1, -1}]}, 1];
tau[0] = ID8; Do[tau[h] = sixAntiSymmetric8by8[[h]], {h, 1, 6}];
tau[7] = tau[1].tau[2].tau[3].tau[4].tau[5].tau[6];
Do[taubar[h] = sigma.Transpose[sigma.tau[h]], {h, 0, 7}];
Do[T16A[A] = ArrayFlatten[{{0, taubar[A]}, {tau[A], 0}}], {A, 0, 7}];
T16A[8] = Dot @@ Table[T16A[A], {A, 0, 7}];          (* chirality  Gamma = T0 \
T1 ... T7 *)
sigma16 = T16A[0].T16A[1].T16A[2].T16A[3];           (* spinor metric of \
dirac16complex *)
PL = (ID16 - T16A[8])/2; PR = (ID16 + T16A[8])/2;    (* chiral projectors *)
SAB = Table[(T16A[A].T16A[B] - T16A[B].T16A[A])/4, {A, 0, 7}, {B, 0, 7}];
Gamma5 = T16A[8];
MatrixForm /@ Table[T16A[A], {A, 0, 7}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d26a23ef-d37d-4dfa-a1d0-a609f287febe"],

