Cell["\<\
Part 7 (appended). Proof that universes of masses {+mass, -mass} are created \
in pairs\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"36519f7d-edef-4283-b223-a67a0dfab1a3"],

Cell["\<\
THEOREM 1 (mass-sign pairing; dirac16complex, all three fields). C: psi -> \
Gamma psi^* and P1: psi(x) -> T^1 psi(R1 x) map every solution of the field \
equation with mass +m onto a solution with mass -m (Part 5.1, exact Grassmann \
identities L_(m)[C psi] = L_(-m)[psi], L_(m)[P1 psi] = L_(-m)[psi]). Both \
maps are involutions (Gamma^2 = I, (T^1)^2 = I), hence bijections: solutions \
come in {+m, -m} pairs.
THEOREM 2 (spectral pairing; all three fields). For every real effective \
potential the Kohn-Sham Hamiltonian obeys T^0 h_KS T^0 = -h_KS and (h_KS)^* = \
-h_KS (Part 6.1); the bag boundary conditions are preserved. Hence every \
Kohn-Sham level eps has a partner -eps: a universe of mass (energy) +eps is \
always accompanied by a universe of mass -eps. The full dirac16complex field \
equation also has real coefficients, so complex conjugation maps a stationary \
solution of frequency eps to one of frequency -eps.
THEOREM 3 (mirror sectors and zero-energy pair creation; every \
x5,x6,x7-independent configuration of dirac16complex). L = L_D[psi_+] - \
L_D[psi_-] - (lam/2)(S_+ - S_-)^2 (Part 3.6). In the zero-energy vacuum V2 \
the total energy is exactly 0 and the two condensates cancel exactly. \
Creating a +universe pair (energy +Delta) together with a -universe pair \
(energy -Delta) leaves rho_s and the Kohn-Sham field unchanged and changes \
the total energy by EXACTLY 0 (Part 6.3, 'dE(both, created together)'). The \
quartic coupling contains the cross term +lam S_+ S_- that connects the \
vacuum to this state (shown below), while the separately conserved charges of \
the two sectors forbid creating a universe alone: universes of masses {+mass, \
-mass} are created in pairs.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4337da5-43d6-4242-af9e-c4f67fd541ef"],

Cell["\<\
Kp = (ID16 + K)/2; Km = (ID16 - K)/2;
psiPlus = gMatVec[Kp, psi]; psiMinus = gMatVec[Km, psi];
psiSPlus = gMatVec[Conjugate[Kp], psiS]; psiSMinus = gMatVec[Conjugate[Km], \
psiS];
Splus = gBil[psiSPlus, betaKS, psiPlus]; Sminus = gBil[psiSMinus, betaKS, \
psiMinus];
crossTerm = gScale[lam, gMul[Splus, Sminus]];
<|\"psibar psi == S_+ - S_-\" -> gZeroQ[gAdd[Sbil, gScale[-1, gAdd[Splus, \
gScale[-1, Sminus]]]]],
 \"(psibar psi)^2 == S_+^2 + S_-^2 - 2 S_+ S_-\" -> gZeroQ[gAdd[gMul[Sbil, \
Sbil], gScale[-1, gAdd[gMul[Splus, Splus], gMul[Sminus, Sminus], gScale[-2, \
gMul[Splus, Sminus]]]]]],
 \"number of monomials in the cross term lam S_+ S_-\" -> Length[crossTerm],
 \"pair energy balance in V2 (all fields)\" -> Table[c -> dftResults[c][\"V2: \
dE(both, created together)\"], {c, Keys[maps]}]|>\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:=",ExpressionUUID->"48225c81-bab7-4035-b60e-56c316e6fb5e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"psibar psi == S_+ - S_-\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"(psibar psi)^2 == S_+^2 + S_-^2 - 2 S_+ S_-\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"number of monomials in the cross term lam S_+ S_-\"\>", "\[Rule]",
     "232"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"pair energy balance in V2 (all fields)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\<\"primordial\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.`"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"modern\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.`"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"future\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0.`"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[30]=",ExpressionUUID->"b40c0519-d449-4649-b9fa-ad27343f7f8a"],

Cell["Part 8 (appended). Einstein-Rosen bridges", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1d2989b5-746b-4eea-b8de-479d86b421a8"],

Cell["\<\
Einstein and Rosen (Phys. Rev. 48, 73 (1935)) replaced r by u with u^2 = r - \
2m in the Schwarzschild metric. The space is then described by two congruent \
sheets (u > 0 and u < 0) joined by the hypersurface u = 0 on which the metric \
determinant g vanishes: the 'bridge'. We verify their two solutions and then \
construct the bridges of the modern and future fields of Part 5 by the same \
substitution; the primordial field is analysed as well.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56be1cf9-a860-4000-ac49-c9a615403814"],

Cell["\<\
christoffelG[g_, xs_] := Module[{gi = Simplify[Inverse[g]], n = Length[xs], \
i, j, k, l},
  Table[Simplify[(1/2) Sum[gi[[i, l]] (D[g[[l, j]], xs[[k]]] + D[g[[l, k]], \
xs[[j]]] - D[g[[j, k]], xs[[l]]]), {l, n}]], {i, n}, {j, n}, {k, n}]];
riemannG[g_, xs_] := Module[{G = christoffelG[g, xs], n = Length[xs], i, j, \
k, l, q},
  Table[Simplify[D[G[[i, j, l]], xs[[k]]] - D[G[[i, j, k]], xs[[l]]] + \
Sum[G[[i, k, q]] G[[q, j, l]] - G[[i, l, q]] G[[q, j, k]], {q, n}]], {i, n}, \
{j, n}, {k, n}, {l, n}]];
ricciG[g_, xs_] := Module[{R = riemannG[g, xs], n = Length[xs], i, j, l}, \
Table[Simplify[Sum[R[[i, j, i, l]], {i, n}]], {j, n}, {l, n}]];
einsteinG[g_, xs_] := Module[{Ric = ricciG[g, xs], Rs}, Rs = \
Simplify[Tr[Inverse[g].Ric]]; Simplify[Ric - (1/2) Rs g]];
kretschmannG[g_, xs_] := Module[{R = riemannG[g, xs], gi = Inverse[g], n = \
Length[xs], i, j, k, l, a, b, c, e},
  Simplify[Sum[g[[i, a]] R[[a, j, k, l]] Sum[gi[[j, b]] gi[[k, c]] gi[[l, e]] \
R[[i, b, c, e]], {b, n}, {c, n}, {e, n}], {i, n}, {a, n}, {j, n}, {k, n}, {l, \
n}]]];
xsER = {t, u, th, ph};
gERneutral = DiagonalMatrix[{-(u^2/(u^2 + 2 mER)), 4 (u^2 + 2 mER), (u^2 + 2 \
mER)^2, (u^2 + 2 mER)^2 Sin[th]^2}];
gERcharged = DiagonalMatrix[{-(u^2/(u^2 + q^2)), 1, u^2 + q^2, (u^2 + q^2) \
Sin[th]^2}];
Fem = ConstantArray[0, {4, 4}]; Fem[[1, 2]] = (q/(u^2 + q^2)) D[Sqrt[u^2 + \
q^2], u]; Fem[[2, 1]] = -Fem[[1, 2]];
TEM = Simplify[(1/(4 Pi)) (Fem.Inverse[gERcharged].Transpose[Fem] - (1/4) \
gERcharged Tr[Inverse[gERcharged].Fem.Inverse[gERcharged].Transpose[Fem]])];
<|\"neutral bridge: Ricci = 0 (vacuum)\" -> (ricciG[gERneutral, xsER] == \
ConstantArray[0, {4, 4}]),
 \"neutral bridge: det g\" -> Simplify[Det[gERneutral]], \"neutral: \
Kretschmann\" -> kretschmannG[gERneutral, xsER],
 \"neutral: two congruent sheets (metric even in u)\" -> ((gERneutral /. u -> \
-u) == gERneutral),
 \"charged bridge (m=0, sign-reversed field energy): G + 8 Pi T = 0\" -> \
(Simplify[einsteinG[gERcharged, xsER] + 8 Pi TEM] == ConstantArray[0, {4, 4}]),
 \"charged: det g at u=0\" -> Simplify[Det[gERcharged] /. u -> 0], \"charged: \
Kretschmann at u=0\" -> Simplify[kretschmannG[gERcharged, xsER] /. u -> 0]|>\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5ebef498-c671-4513-ab18-44f6ca0ebab7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"neutral bridge: Ricci = 0 (vacuum)\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], 
   ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"neutral bridge: det g\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "4"}], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["u", "2"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "mER"}], "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["u", "2"]}], ")"}], "4"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "th", "]"}], "2"]}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"neutral: Kretschmann\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"48", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["mER", "2"]}], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "mER"}], "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["u", "2"]}], ")"}], "6"]]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"neutral: two congruent sheets (metric even in u)\"\>", "\[Rule]",
     "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"charged bridge (m=0, sign-reversed field energy): G + 8 Pi T \
= 0\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"charged: det g at u=0\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"charged: Kretschmann at u=0\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    FractionBox["56", 
     SuperscriptBox["q", "4"]]}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[31]=",ExpressionUUID->"1091f436-7888-4517-bcf2-a1a4a1cc24d3"],

Cell["8.1 Bridges of the modern and future gravitational fields", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e5ae2d55-ee88-44ee-8b6f-933b0c733d9b"],

Cell["\<\
The (x0, x4) part of the modern and future fields is ds^2 = dx0^2/f - f dx4^2 \
with f(x_h) = 0 at a horizon. The Einstein-Rosen substitution x0 = x_h + s \
u^2 (s = +1 for a black-hole horizon with f'(x_h) > 0, s = -1 for a \
cosmological horizon with f'(x_h) < 0) gives g_uu = 4 u^2/f -> 4/|f'(x_h)| \
(regular), g_44 = -f -> 0 (the bridge hypersurface u = 0, where g vanishes), \
and a metric even in u (two congruent sheets). The full 8D metric is this 2D \
metric times the flat (3,3) transverse space, so its curvature invariants are \
those of the 2D part: R = -f''(x0), finite at the bridge.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"42e34c18-b62b-4a5a-bfbb-b9c16a2c1bdd"],

Cell["\<\
bridge[f_, xh_, s_] := Module[{x0u = xh + s u^2, guu, g44},
  guu = 4 u^2/(f /. x0 -> x0u); g44 = -(f /. x0 -> x0u);
  <|\"g_uu at u=0 (= 4/(s f'(x_h)))\" -> Simplify[RootReduce[4/(s D[f, x0] /. \
x0 -> xh)]], \"check: g_uu at u=10^-6\" -> N[guu /. u -> 10^-6, 12],
    \"g_44 at u=0\" -> RootReduce[Simplify[g44 /. u -> 0]], \"metric even in \
u\" -> (Simplify[(guu /. u -> -u) - guu] == 0 && Simplify[(g44 /. u -> -u) - \
g44] == 0),
    \"Ricci scalar at u=0 (= -f''(x_h))\" -> N[-D[f, {x0, 2}] /. x0 -> xh, \
10], \"surface gravity kappa = |f'(x_h)|/2\" -> N[Abs[D[f, x0] /. x0 -> \
xh]/2, 10]|>];
fFexact = 1 - 1/x0 - x0^2/100;                     (* future field with rs = \
1, HL = 1/10, exact *)
horizonsFexact = Sort[x0 /. Solve[x0 fFexact == 0 && x0 > 0, x0, Reals]];
bridgeModern = bridge[1 - rs/x0, rs, +1];
bridgeFutureBH = bridge[fFexact, horizonsFexact[[1]], +1];
bridgeFutureCosmo = bridge[fFexact, horizonsFexact[[2]], -1];
<|\"modern (black-hole horizon x0 = rs)\" -> bridgeModern, \"future, \
black-hole horizon\" -> bridgeFutureBH, \"future, cosmological horizon\" -> \
bridgeFutureCosmo|>\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:=",ExpressionUUID->"aa16add3-7973-46b3-b0be-f0b3f3414f8e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"modern (black-hole horizon x0 = rs)\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\<\"g_uu at u=0 (= 4/(s f'(x_h)))\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"4", " ", "rs"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"check: g_uu at u=10^-6\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       FractionBox["4.`12.*^-12", 
        RowBox[{"1.`12.", "-", 
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"1.`12.", " ", "rs"}], 
          RowBox[{"1.`12.*^-12", "+", "rs"}]]}]]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"g_44 at u=0\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"metric even in u\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Ricci scalar at u=0 (= -f''(x_h))\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       FractionBox["2.`10.", 
        SuperscriptBox["rs", "2"]]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"surface gravity kappa = |f'(x_h)|/2\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       FractionBox["0.5`10.", 
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "rs", "]"}]]}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]}], ",", 
   
   RowBox[{"\<\"future, black-hole horizon\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\<\"g_uu at u=0 (= 4/(s f'(x_h)))\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       TemplateBox[<|"icon" -> "Root", "small" -> InterpretationBox[
           StyleBox[
            TemplateBox[{"\"4.17\"", 
              DynamicBox[
               FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
               "FEExpressions", "NumericalApproximationElider"]]}, 
             "RowDefault"], ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
           4.16891046301191448009149098652414977551`15.954589770191003, 
           Editable -> False], "approx" -> 4.1689104630119145`, "interp" -> 
         InterpretationBox["", 
           Root[640000 - 160000 # + 373 #^3& , 2, 0]], "head" -> "Root", 
         "big" -> RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"640000", "-", 
              RowBox[{"160000", " ", "#1"}], "+", 
              RowBox[{"373", " ", 
                SuperscriptBox["#1", "3"]}]}], "&"}], "degree" -> "3", 
         "shortDegree" -> "3", "number" -> 2|>,
        "NumericalApproximationInterp"]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"check: g_uu at u=10^-6\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       "4.16891046301617075619556600051897297895`12."}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"g_44 at u=0\"\>", "\[Rule]", "0"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"metric even in u\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"Ricci scalar at u=0 (= -f''(x_h))\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       "1.9593791182857592155433599165724902973`10."}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\<\"surface gravity kappa = |f'(x_h)|/2\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
       "0.47974165378333872211700454502174326829`10."}]}], 
     "\[RightAssociation]"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"future, cosmological horizon\"\>", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
